pared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   in this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  the results of immunohistochemical staining for progesterone receptor protein are for investigational use only  they must not be used for clinical purposes  added by  frederick carl koerner  m d  signed on  23 removed_month 94 at 10 46 gross description  received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled remove_patient_name  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a removed_date x removed_date x 1 2cm fragment of yellow breast tissue  with localization wire in place  an x ray accompanies this specimen  the specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an irregular firm  white lesion measuring removed_date x removed_date x 0 6cm  grossly within 1mm of an inked resection margin  a representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  and resubmitted in g  remainder of tissue in a f  resident  douglas b  flieder  md     intra operative diagnosis     frozen section diagnosis  1   breast left  biopsy  infiltrating ductal carcinoma  o r  resident  kathleen o neil smith  bums o r  diagnosis by  austin l  vickery  m d                                                                                  source care unit  surgical day care   acc 3 reports to  leslie wayne ottinger  m d  part   left breast   report_end  , No.
