body contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  the results of immunohistochemical staining for progesterone receptor protein are for investigational use only  they must not be used for clinical purposes  added by  frederick carl koerner  m d  signed on  09 removed_month 94 at 13 02 gross description  received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled remove_patient_name  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast biopsy  is a removed_date x removed_date x 1 9cm  white and yellow fibrofatty portion of breast tissue  the specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a mixture of adipose tissue  and white  semi rubbery fibrous tissue  there is no grossly suspicious lesion for infiltrating carcinoma that is large enough to freeze  no frozen section is done  the specimen is submitted entirely in a through h  resident  stamatina kaptain  md     intra operative diagnosis     gross diagnosis  breast right excision  ill  defined firm area  somewhat suspicious for invasive tumor  but too small to freeze  specimen to be processed only for permanents  o r  resident  scott d  urban  hms o r  diagnosis by  john h  eichhorn  m d                                                                                  source care unit  surgical day care   acc 3 reports to  barbara lynn smith  m d  part   right breast mass   report_end  , No.
